Origin
------

A port to Apple platforms of the Android application "CIEreader"
(cauer71/AndroidDev, apps/cie-reader), by the same two authors. The data model,
the three parsers, the archive format, the export field names and all
user-facing wording come from there. See COPYRIGHT for what was carried over and
what was written for this platform.

Names
-----

"IDReader" and "CIEreader" are the names these two applications go by. Section 6
of the License does not grant permission to use them. Take the code; give your
build its own name.

What this software is not
-------------------------

It reads identity documents and reports whether the chip's signatures check out.
It is not a legal instrument and gives no legal advice. Whoever deploys it is the
controller of the personal data it processes and answers for the lawfulness of
that processing — see the first-run notice inside the app and
docs/DATA-PROTECTION.md.

A judgement of "genuine" says that the cryptography checked out. It does not say
that the person in front of you is the person in the document.

